{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCB3gmC8skU9dnWVTbJro2","type":"tool_result","content":"3:*Generated from `draft-v1.md` (draft-voice.md does not exist at this stage; all line numbers cite `../Book-KCNA/.pipeline-state/ch-15/draft-v1.md`). Every ASCII diagram in the draft must have an entry here; every entry must correspond to an anchor in the draft.*\n7:**Anchor-to-block correspondence:** 1:1. Every fence opens on the line immediately after its anchor.\n11:## UNANCHORED DIAGRAMS\n13:None. All seven fenced blocks in the draft carry a preceding `<!-- FIGURE: ... -->` anchor.\n17:## FIGURE-CONTRACT FLAGS\n22:`ch15-zenith-control-loop-pointed-at-a-repo` (line 968) substitutes `zenith` for `fig{MM}`. Rule 4 requires `ch{NN}-fig{MM}-{kebab-slug}`; the other six anchors in the chapter conform. The conforming form would be `ch15-fig07-zenith-control-loop-pointed-at-a-repo`. Until this is resolved the book-level aggregator will either drop the figure or index it under a non-conforming key. The spec below uses the ID as written.\n25:`ch15-fig05-opengitops-four-principles` (line 473) is captioned **Figure 15.4**; `ch15-fig04-argocd-sync-states-and-hooks` (line 610) is captioned **Figure 15.5**. The anchors also appear in the draft in the order 05-then-04. Independently caught by the fact-accuracy diagnostic (item 13). The anchor is the join key, so swapping the two printed caption numbers is the cheaper fix; renumbering the anchors is the other. Author's call.\n28:`ch15-fig04-argocd-sync-states-and-hooks` depicts sync states only. Hooks are in `ch15-fig06-sync-waves-and-hook-phases`. The spec below is written to the drawn content, not to the slug. **Do not add hook nodes to satisfy the slug.**\n33:(a) Figure 15.7's caption instructs the reader to \"Lay this beside Figure 3.2.\" Chapter 3 as shipped (`chapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md`) carries no numbered figure captions at all — only chapters 6 and 8 use that convention. **\"Figure 3.2\" has no referent in the book.** The figure meant is anchor `ch03-fig02-control-loop-desired-vs-current` (`chapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md:762`).\n37:Three resolutions, in descending order of what they preserve: redraw `ch03-fig02` onto the Chapter 15 chassis and reflow the Chapter 3 prose around it (preserves the payoff; costs a Chapter 3 edit); redraw `ch15-fig07` onto Chapter 3's chassis (cheaper, but loses the API-server node that §3's Navigational Hazards block depends on); or soften Figure 15.7's caption to a family resemblance. **Whichever is chosen, the two figures must be commissioned and rendered as a pair, on one chassis, so they superimpose.**\n43:`ch15-fig03` uses 🔑 (U+1F511) at lines 418 and 429. Harmless in source — the fence is replaced by the rendered asset at build — but the *rendered* asset must use a drawn key, never the emoji. Astral-plane glyphs render as empty boxes on Kindle.\n50:## Figure: ch15-fig01-twelve-factor-in-kubernetes\n52:**Anchor ID:** `ch15-fig01-twelve-factor-in-kubernetes`\n93:**Proposed filename:** `ch15-fig01-twelve-factor-in-kubernetes.png`\n96:anchor_id: ch15-fig01-twelve-factor-in-kubernetes\n135:## Figure: ch15-fig02-deployment-strategies-compared\n137:**Anchor ID:** `ch15-fig02-deployment-strategies-compared`\n197:**Proposed filename:** `ch15-fig02-deployment-strategies-compared.png`\n200:anchor_id: ch15-fig02-deployment-strategies-compared\n251:## Figure: ch15-fig03-cicd-push-vs-gitops-pull\n253:**Anchor ID:** `ch15-fig03-cicd-push-vs-gitops-pull`\n310:**Proposed filename:** `ch15-fig03-cicd-push-vs-gitops-pull.png`\n313:anchor_id: ch15-fig03-cicd-push-vs-gitops-pull\n360:## Figure: ch15-fig05-opengitops-four-principles\n362:**Anchor ID:** `ch15-fig05-opengitops-four-principles`\n418:**Proposed filename:** `ch15-fig05-opengitops-four-principles.png`\n421:anchor_id: ch15-fig05-opengitops-four-principles\n467:## Figure: ch15-fig04-argocd-sync-states-and-hooks\n469:**Anchor ID:** `ch15-fig04-argocd-sync-states-and-hooks